WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.467 --> 00:00:11.040
♪♪ INTRO ♪♪

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:21.200
A little over three years ago, I saw a video
on YouTube of a cell dying and I loved it

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.740
so much that I reached out to the 
person who posted that video.

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:28.320
His name was James, and in that email, 
I wrote the following:

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:32.910
“I have always wanted to do a microscopy
show, we've just lacked the expertise.

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:37.321
You have something pretty special on your
hands, an obvious passion, talent,

00:00:37.321 --> 00:00:38.390
and the right equipment.

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:42.090
I'm interested in possibly partnering with
you on a channel. I'm thinking of

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:46.180
something that has a real chill look and feel.
Something that celebrates 

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:52.550
the beauty of that world, gives people 
a chance to relax while also learning.”

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:56.010
James agreed.

00:00:56.010 --> 00:01:02.540
It is unusual for an idea to go from inception
to execution with so little modification.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:07.430
That first pitch is very much what this channel
continues to be today.

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:10.890
Aside from the original idea for the name
of the channel which was…

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:12.619
The Germ House.

00:01:14.551 --> 00:01:17.760
Through the years, there have been some very
exciting developments.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:21.149
James has been able to upgrade his microscope
multiple times.

00:01:21.149 --> 00:01:24.880
We’ve been able to share marine life as
well as fresh water.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:31.717
We’ve captured some truly exceptional moments
and even, we think, discovered entirely new species.

00:01:31.759 --> 00:01:36.619
But also, how I have thought about microscopy
has changed.

00:01:36.619 --> 00:01:41.670
Before I found James’ footage, I wanted
to make microscopy content but I thought I couldn't.

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:45.959
There were so many microscopes, and so
many different words I didn’t know.

00:01:45.959 --> 00:01:50.579
I honestly didn't even know 
what a ciliate was!

00:01:50.579 --> 00:01:55.399
As I watched more and more footage, and narrated
more and more episodes, I started to understand

00:01:55.399 --> 00:01:59.079
that this isn’t something that’s just
for experts.

00:01:59.079 --> 00:02:02.740
Obviously, I will never be as accomplished
as James.

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:07.240
But after getting my own Microcosmos Microscope
as part of our Kickstarter, I found that this

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:14.209
was an extremely fulfilling and also fairly
accessible hobby.

00:02:14.209 --> 00:02:21.750
Spending time in my neighborhood understanding
my local microcosmos has been very exciting.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:27.470
The changing ecology of the seasons, my first
tardigrade sighting, and just the variety

00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:31.250
of life at different depths of water and sediment.

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:35.401
The Microcosmos Microscope changed my whole
outlook on this channel.

00:02:35.401 --> 00:02:40.199
It’s not just a project that tells people
about their world, we hope it is an

00:02:40.199 --> 00:02:44.069
invitation into that world.

00:02:44.069 --> 00:02:50.069
There are so many more people with telescopes
than microscopes, but, no offense to all of

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:53.183
the backyard astronomers out there, there
is so much more to see

00:02:53.183 --> 00:02:55.519
looking down than looking up.

00:02:55.519 --> 00:03:01.000
And we want to help more people start their
own journeys, so they can explore the unseen

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:03.510
world that surrounds them.

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:09.421
So that’s why we launched the Microcosmos
Microscope Kickstarter in early 2021, and

00:03:09.421 --> 00:03:14.980
we made sure to offer a high quality introductory
microscope, with a cell-phone adapter, so

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:17.409
the everybody could document their own journeys.

00:03:17.409 --> 00:03:23.665
And the people who supported that kickstarter
have enabled the next step we are taking today

00:03:23.665 --> 00:03:26.717
the launch of Microcosmos.store.

00:03:30.997 --> 00:03:35.030
This new store exists to welcome folks on
their own journeys.

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:39.140
Right now, we’ve got a fairly limited number
of Microcosmos Microscopes available, but

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:43.539
we will be restocking them later this year,
so get them while they're hot.

00:03:43.539 --> 00:03:48.390
We’ll also be increasing the number
of microscopy tools and accessories we offer.

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:52.629
Right now, along with the microscope, you can
get things like Rheinberg filters, oblique

00:03:52.629 --> 00:03:58.740
illumination filters, slides and coverslips,
our microscopy field guide, and a Microcosmos

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:00.050
microfiber cleaning cloth.

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:05.079
We even have a series of instructional videos
explaining how to get started with both the

00:04:05.079 --> 00:04:08.400
equipment and sampling your local microcosmos.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:13.249
Also, of course, we’ve got some cool stuff
that you can get to represent your appreciation

00:04:13.249 --> 00:04:14.810
for the microcosmos.

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:19.440
You can download our soundtrack to listen
to while you search your slides, or cozy up

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:21.470
in our new Lacrymaria socks.

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:26.900
We’ve also got a glow-in-the-dark tardigrade
pin, a very cool and clever sweatshirt, and

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:30.164
this new hydra t-shirt is just fantastic.

00:04:30.164 --> 00:04:35.420
And finally, possibly my favorite thing is
this poster, with art by one of James’ mentors

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:39.350
that will help you identify the microbes you
find in your samples.

00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:44.592
It has over 100 species on it and it also
just looks really really cool.

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:53.530
In case it’s not clear to you, we really
have been going on a journey together.

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:59.290
And I’m not just saying words when I say
thank you for coming on it with us.

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:04.100
I am so grateful to have had this richness
added to my life.

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:10.000
A new and deep appreciation for something
that was, just a few short years ago, the

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:13.120
unseen world that surrounds me.

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:17.450
Now before we go, we’d also like to thank each
and every one of our Patreon patrons.

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:22.020
Without whom this channel and this store
could not exist and we are so so grateful

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:25.540
for all of you who have decided to sign up
over at patreon.com/journeytomicro.

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:31.120
If you’d like to see more from our Master
of Microscopes James Weiss, check him

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:33.480
out at Jam &amp; Germs on Instagram.

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:38.070
And if you’d like to see more from us, there’s
probably a subscribe button somewhere nearby.

